WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.151 --> 00:00:03.603
- Hey legal eagles, aah
the age old question of how

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.676
to choose the right law school.

00:00:05.676 --> 00:00:08.603
Currently there are over
250 different law schools

00:00:08.603 --> 00:00:12.366
in the U.S. alone and choosing
between them can be daunting.

00:00:12.366 --> 00:00:14.397
But today we're gonna go
over the main concerns

00:00:14.397 --> 00:00:16.190
that you should consider when deciding

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.703
between law schools so stick around.

00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:21.286
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.128 --> 00:00:26.417
There are a number of factors
to consider when choosing

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:29.991
between law schools and
no one size fits all

00:00:29.991 --> 00:00:33.295
but the first consideration
is what job do you want

00:00:33.295 --> 00:00:35.210
when you graduate from law school?

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:38.877
Certain jobs require a pedigree
and others not so much.

00:00:38.877 --> 00:00:40.187
There's no way around it

00:00:40.187 --> 00:00:43.342
but sometimes law school rank matters.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.599
Lots of people pay attention to it.

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:47.349
If you want to be a supreme court clerk

00:00:47.349 --> 00:00:50.209
and then parlay that
clerkship into a big firm

00:00:50.209 --> 00:00:52.697
litigation job, well
that requires the highest

00:00:52.697 --> 00:00:54.950
law school pedigree that's out there.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.453
You need to go to a top law school.

00:00:57.453 --> 00:00:59.295
Other jobs, on the
other hand, like working

00:00:59.295 --> 00:01:02.208
for a small or medium
sized law firm often don't

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:05.634
require as much pedigree
or a top law school rank.

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:08.621
Some jobs don't require
really any pedigree at all

00:01:08.621 --> 00:01:11.271
and in fact sometimes you can
get into a district attorney

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.335
job or a public defender's
job without the same kind

00:01:13.335 --> 00:01:16.867
of pedigree of a top law
school that would be necessary

00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:20.820
to become a big firm litigator
or a supreme court clerk.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.509
So before you think about
how you want to get there

00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:26.352
think about where you want to go.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.222
It's important to know the destination

00:01:28.222 --> 00:01:30.716
before you choose the right path.

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:33.034
If your ideal job requires
a top law school, well then

00:01:33.034 --> 00:01:35.234
you'll want to aim for a top law school.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.142
The next factor I would
take into consideration

00:01:37.142 --> 00:01:40.335
is the geographical location
of where you want to practice.

00:01:40.335 --> 00:01:42.909
Certainly it's no surprise
that top law schools

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:45.616
probably open up the
most options but often

00:01:45.616 --> 00:01:48.820
if you want to work in a
specific geographical region

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:51.558
there are certain regional law
schools that are considered

00:01:51.558 --> 00:01:53.979
just as good as many of the
better ranked law schools

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:57.751
for the purposes of that
particular geographical location.

00:01:57.751 --> 00:02:00.417
Certain regional law schools
punch way about their weight

00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:02.561
for the region that they're located in.

00:02:02.561 --> 00:02:05.388
If you know you wanna end
up in a particular location

00:02:05.388 --> 00:02:08.466
you might go to a law school in that area.

00:02:08.466 --> 00:02:11.344
The alumni network might be
well connected in that area.

00:02:11.344 --> 00:02:14.502
You might be able to get
more networking opportunities

00:02:14.502 --> 00:02:17.553
in that city or that state
so in certain circumstances,

00:02:17.553 --> 00:02:20.432
a regional law school can have advantages

00:02:20.432 --> 00:02:22.556
over a higher ranked law school.

00:02:22.556 --> 00:02:24.666
So for example, if you
knew you wanted to practice

00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:27.559
in Los Angeles, California,
you might consider going

00:02:27.559 --> 00:02:32.420
to Loyola or Pepperdine in
the LA area and while they're

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.136
not the top ranked law
schools in the country,

00:02:35.136 --> 00:02:38.229
they punch above their weight
in the Los Angeles area.

00:02:38.229 --> 00:02:41.028
By the same token however,
going to a much higher

00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:43.431
ranked law school might open
up even more opportunities

00:02:43.431 --> 00:02:46.712
in a wider geographical
location and frankly

00:02:46.712 --> 00:02:48.732
if you go to some of the top
law schools then it shouldn't

00:02:48.732 --> 00:02:52.703
be too difficult to get a job
in any particular location.

00:02:52.703 --> 00:02:54.787
But that's always something
to consider especially if

00:02:54.787 --> 00:02:58.104
different law schools offer
different financial packages

00:02:58.104 --> 00:03:00.078
and financial aid as well.

00:03:00.078 --> 00:03:02.399
Sometimes going to a
regional school can save you

00:03:02.399 --> 00:03:05.615
a lot of money but you have
to weigh the pros and cons

00:03:05.615 --> 00:03:08.590
versus going to a better
ranked school that might

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.226
open up more doors outside
of just a particular

00:03:11.226 --> 00:03:14.121
geographical location and
sometimes people decide

00:03:14.121 --> 00:03:17.333
that they don't wanna stay
in a particular city or state

00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:19.238
and they wanna move to somewhere else.

00:03:19.238 --> 00:03:21.675
Going to a higher ranked
school can sometimes open up

00:03:21.675 --> 00:03:24.509
those kind of opportunities
which brings me

00:03:24.509 --> 00:03:26.319
to the next factor that
you should probably

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:28.347
consider when deciding between law schools

00:03:28.347 --> 00:03:31.173
and that's how much
are you willing to pay?

00:03:31.173 --> 00:03:33.209
Unfortunately there's not
much difference in terms

00:03:33.209 --> 00:03:36.452
of the public or rack rates that you see

00:03:36.452 --> 00:03:38.879
from different law schools
and the amount that you pay

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:41.861
doesn't really correlate
to the rank of that school.

00:03:41.861 --> 00:03:44.971
In fact it's often inversely
correlated where the

00:03:44.971 --> 00:03:47.168
better schools actually
charge less than some of the

00:03:47.168 --> 00:03:50.047
lower ranked schools and some
of the for profit schools

00:03:50.047 --> 00:03:53.829
charge the most out of
everybody but there's really not

00:03:53.829 --> 00:03:57.140
a huge amount of variation
between the published rates

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:01.123
of the highest ranked schools
and the lowest ranked schools.

00:04:01.123 --> 00:04:03.149
But that doesn't mean
there's no difference at all.

00:04:03.149 --> 00:04:06.010
Generally speaking, public
law schools are going

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.338
to charge less, often tens
of thousands of dollars

00:04:08.338 --> 00:04:12.124
less per year than their
private counterparts but the

00:04:12.124 --> 00:04:15.314
biggest difference comes in
the form of financial aid.

00:04:15.314 --> 00:04:18.270
Just because the published
tuition is high doesn't mean

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.299
that students are actually
going to pay that much.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:23.068
There's often a huge amount
of competition amongst

00:04:23.068 --> 00:04:26.590
law schools to attract the best
and brightest law students.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:29.050
So different law schools
offer a huge variation

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.987
in financial aid which can
sometimes result in scholarships

00:04:31.987 --> 00:04:36.066
from a few hundred dollars
to several thousand dollars

00:04:36.066 --> 00:04:39.018
or even full rides and full ride pluses.

00:04:39.018 --> 00:04:40.746
It can result in a huge difference

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.505
in the amount that you
pay at the end of the day

00:04:42.505 --> 00:04:44.001
when you go to law school.

00:04:44.001 --> 00:04:46.064
So often you have to make a
decision between going to a

00:04:46.064 --> 00:04:48.752
higher ranked law school or
going to one that's going

00:04:48.752 --> 00:04:51.594
to pay you more money to go
there and when you're talking

00:04:51.594 --> 00:04:55.709
about law school where tuition
alone can cost $50,000 a year

00:04:55.709 --> 00:04:58.714
not to mention living
expenses, it's not surprising

00:04:58.714 --> 00:05:02.043
that law students often
graduate with over $200,000

00:05:02.043 --> 00:05:04.048
in law school debt alone.

00:05:04.048 --> 00:05:06.164
So getting a large financial aid package

00:05:06.164 --> 00:05:08.359
can have a huge effect on your quality

00:05:08.359 --> 00:05:10.312
of life when you graduate from law school.

00:05:10.312 --> 00:05:12.624
Another factor to consider
is do you want to go

00:05:12.624 --> 00:05:15.040
into a specialty in the law?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.057
What most people don't
know is that law schools

00:05:17.057 --> 00:05:19.754
teach basically the same thing especially

00:05:19.754 --> 00:05:23.013
in your first year and
usually into your second year

00:05:23.013 --> 00:05:25.381
and unfortunately no law
school really prepares

00:05:25.381 --> 00:05:27.890
you for practicing as an attorney.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.170
No one feels ready to
practice when they graduate

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.176
from law school and
that's true whether you go

00:05:32.176 --> 00:05:34.082
to the number one law
school in the country

00:05:34.082 --> 00:05:37.011
or the number 100th law
school in the country.

00:05:37.011 --> 00:05:41.251
It's shocking but they all
teach basically the same thing

00:05:41.251 --> 00:05:44.175
but a handful of schools
really excel in a few specialty

00:05:44.175 --> 00:05:49.175
areas like tax or entertainment
law or law and economics.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.505
So if you know that you
wanna go into one of these

00:05:51.505 --> 00:05:54.014
specialty fields, generally
the kind of fields

00:05:54.014 --> 00:05:56.833
that require an LLM or
a masters of the law

00:05:56.833 --> 00:05:59.340
then you might consider
going to one of those schools

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.882
that really excels in
that area but outside

00:06:01.882 --> 00:06:05.230
of those really specialty
areas, I would not assume

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.146
that any law school is going
to teach you anything different

00:06:08.146 --> 00:06:10.492
from another law school
and unless you're going

00:06:10.492 --> 00:06:14.244
into one of those LLM type
areas, odds are you're gonna

00:06:14.244 --> 00:06:17.581
get the exact same
education as anywhere else.

00:06:17.581 --> 00:06:19.621
There aren't that many areas in which this

00:06:19.621 --> 00:06:23.893
specialty applies, tax is the
one that really comes out.

00:06:23.893 --> 00:06:25.802
So if you know that you
wanna go into one of these

00:06:25.802 --> 00:06:29.094
specialty fields that requires
an advanced law degree

00:06:29.094 --> 00:06:30.757
then you might consider
going to a law school

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:34.416
that has a very high ranked
specialty program in that area.

00:06:34.416 --> 00:06:37.363
The next big consideration
when thinking about law schools

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:40.560
is whether you want to go into big law.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.171
Most students think that
they want to go into big law

00:06:43.171 --> 00:06:45.111
when they start law school
whether it's actually

00:06:45.111 --> 00:06:47.815
the best thing for them or
not and while it's certainly

00:06:47.815 --> 00:06:51.013
not the route for everyone,
it is the route that I took.

00:06:51.013 --> 00:06:53.069
I've been a big firm
lawyer for over 10 years.

00:06:53.069 --> 00:06:56.075
I've recruited, I have
mentored summer associates

00:06:56.075 --> 00:06:58.817
and here's what I think
are the most important

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:01.184
takeaways if you wanna go into big law

00:07:01.184 --> 00:07:03.680
when you're deciding between law schools.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.816
If you wanna go the big firm route you

00:07:05.816 --> 00:07:07.352
generally need to go to
one of the best schools

00:07:07.352 --> 00:07:10.054
in the country, the most
prestigious schools.

00:07:10.054 --> 00:07:13.093
At the top of the 250 law
schools in the country

00:07:13.093 --> 00:07:14.864
there are three at the very top that are

00:07:14.864 --> 00:07:17.807
always changing in position for number one

00:07:17.807 --> 00:07:20.360
and that's usually Yale,
Harvard and Stanford.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.719
Which one of those three
schools is ranked number one

00:07:22.719 --> 00:07:26.795
in a particular year largely
depends on who you ask

00:07:26.795 --> 00:07:28.874
but generally those three
schools are considered

00:07:28.874 --> 00:07:31.162
the top three schools in the country.

00:07:31.162 --> 00:07:34.006
If you're able to get
into the roughly top half

00:07:34.006 --> 00:07:36.423
of your class at one
of the top law schools

00:07:36.423 --> 00:07:38.384
in the country, you
stand a very good chance

00:07:38.384 --> 00:07:42.094
of being competitive with
the top firms in the country

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:44.135
and getting a big firm job.

00:07:44.135 --> 00:07:46.124
Now apart from the top three law schools

00:07:46.124 --> 00:07:48.154
there are what people generally refer

00:07:48.154 --> 00:07:51.405
to as the top tier of
law schools, often called

00:07:51.405 --> 00:07:54.590
the tier one law schools
or T14 law schools.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.891
Those are also almost
universally considered the

00:07:57.891 --> 00:08:02.314
top law schools in the
country, roughly the top 10%.

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:05.215
You'll hear people talk
about the top 14 law schools

00:08:05.215 --> 00:08:06.479
in the country, sometimes it's the top 15

00:08:06.479 --> 00:08:09.065
and sometimes it's the top 20.

00:08:09.065 --> 00:08:10.933
Really there's not a
whole lot of difference

00:08:10.933 --> 00:08:13.676
between those top tier schools.

00:08:13.676 --> 00:08:16.300
Those top 10% of law
schools are schools like

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:20.300
NYU, Berkeley, UCLA,
Georgetown, Michigan, Duke,

00:08:21.365 --> 00:08:23.994
Columbia, I'm also
leaving out a whole bunch

00:08:23.994 --> 00:08:27.021
of those top tier schools
but they're generally

00:08:27.021 --> 00:08:29.861
considered the top schools in the country.

00:08:29.861 --> 00:08:31.759
Even though you're in one
of the top law schools

00:08:31.759 --> 00:08:34.151
of the country you still
need to do reasonably well

00:08:34.151 --> 00:08:37.203
in your class in order
to get a big firm job

00:08:37.203 --> 00:08:39.578
but if you're safely in
the top third of your class

00:08:39.578 --> 00:08:42.332
at a tier one school, you
stand a very good chance

00:08:42.332 --> 00:08:44.627
of getting a big firm job or a clerkship.

00:08:44.627 --> 00:08:46.953
After that, I would say
that there is sort of a

00:08:46.953 --> 00:08:48.598
second tier of law schools.

00:08:48.598 --> 00:08:52.697
The law schools ranked
generally between 20 and 100.

00:08:52.697 --> 00:08:54.349
If you go to one of these
schools and you want

00:08:54.349 --> 00:08:56.251
to go the big firm
route, generally you have

00:08:56.251 --> 00:08:59.263
to be in the top five
to 10% of your class.

00:08:59.263 --> 00:09:01.857
You have to do very well
at these tier two schools

00:09:01.857 --> 00:09:03.825
in order to get the most competitive jobs

00:09:03.825 --> 00:09:06.200
because you're competing
with thousands of people

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.602
that went to the top
tier schools and you have

00:09:08.602 --> 00:09:10.736
to demonstrate that you are above the rest

00:09:10.736 --> 00:09:13.957
of your class so it can be very difficult.

00:09:13.957 --> 00:09:16.458
If you want to go to a
law school that is outside

00:09:16.458 --> 00:09:20.205
the top 100 and you still
wanna go the prestigious

00:09:20.205 --> 00:09:22.373
big firm route, well it's still possible

00:09:22.373 --> 00:09:25.033
but you're really going
to have to differentiate

00:09:25.033 --> 00:09:27.013
yourself from the rest of your class.

00:09:27.013 --> 00:09:30.501
You really have to excel
and be roughly the top

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:33.447
one or two people, maybe
the top five in your class

00:09:33.447 --> 00:09:36.840
in order to get the kind of
ranking that would allow you

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.232
to get the big firm jobs.

00:09:38.232 --> 00:09:40.736
These are the kind of rankings
and grades that are also

00:09:40.736 --> 00:09:42.965
going to let you transfer
to a different school

00:09:42.965 --> 00:09:46.211
if you wanna go that route
but keep in mind that

00:09:46.211 --> 00:09:48.771
big law is not all there is.

00:09:48.771 --> 00:09:52.059
There's all kinds of jobs in
law and you shouldn't assume

00:09:52.059 --> 00:09:55.960
that big law is necessarily
the right one for you.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.680
You've gotta work thousands
of hours and it can

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.430
really burn you out so don't
just assume that big law

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:03.625
is the one and only route in law school.

00:10:03.625 --> 00:10:05.305
There's lots of different
careers in the legal field

00:10:05.305 --> 00:10:08.285
and you may not want to go
into big law in particular.

00:10:08.285 --> 00:10:10.471
Additionally, when you're
thinking about different careers

00:10:10.471 --> 00:10:13.755
in law check out the data
that the ABA puts out

00:10:13.755 --> 00:10:15.166
on different law schools.

00:10:15.166 --> 00:10:18.185
The ABA publishes information
on each school that will tell

00:10:18.185 --> 00:10:20.613
you how successful their
graduates are, what states

00:10:20.613 --> 00:10:23.825
that those graduates practice
in and it will also tell you

00:10:23.825 --> 00:10:26.833
the average income that
graduates from that particular

00:10:26.833 --> 00:10:30.118
law school make so don't
just rely on generalities

00:10:30.118 --> 00:10:34.260
but really dig in and see if
graduates from the law school

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:37.476
that you're considering are
going into the kind of jobs

00:10:37.476 --> 00:10:39.407
that you really want to go into.

00:10:39.407 --> 00:10:42.040
So that being said, while
everyone's situation is different

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.428
and there's never a general
best law school for everyone,

00:10:45.428 --> 00:10:47.843
I do wanna give you some general tips.

00:10:47.843 --> 00:10:49.439
All things being equal, I would say go

00:10:49.439 --> 00:10:51.158
to a higher ranked law school.

00:10:51.158 --> 00:10:53.316
The higher ranked law schools,
especially when you get

00:10:53.316 --> 00:10:56.588
into the top tier of law
schools really open up many

00:10:56.588 --> 00:10:59.131
different options for you
and maybe a year from now

00:10:59.131 --> 00:11:01.344
when you're a two L or three
years from now, what you

00:11:01.344 --> 00:11:04.233
want out of your legal
career might be completely

00:11:04.233 --> 00:11:06.894
different than what you
want when you start out

00:11:06.894 --> 00:11:11.557
so going to a higher ranked
law firm, often if there's

00:11:11.557 --> 00:11:14.083
a big difference in the
ranking, can really open up

00:11:14.083 --> 00:11:16.507
some different options if not now then

00:11:16.507 --> 00:11:18.126
perhaps later down the line.

00:11:18.126 --> 00:11:20.992
So all things being
equal, you might consider

00:11:20.992 --> 00:11:23.111
a higher ranked law school.

00:11:23.111 --> 00:11:25.787
Also again all things being
equal, you might consider going

00:11:25.787 --> 00:11:28.252
to a school that offers
more financial aid.

00:11:28.252 --> 00:11:31.966
If you're deciding between
schools within the top tier

00:11:31.966 --> 00:11:35.725
or within the top three in
the top tier and one school

00:11:35.725 --> 00:11:38.224
gives you a full ride and
another school gives you

00:11:38.224 --> 00:11:40.844
zero financial aid, I would
probably choose the one

00:11:40.844 --> 00:11:43.665
that gives you more financial
aid despite the fact

00:11:43.665 --> 00:11:46.253
that there might be a 10
rank difference between

00:11:46.253 --> 00:11:48.132
school number one and school number 10.

00:11:48.132 --> 00:11:50.181
There's probably not going to be that much

00:11:50.181 --> 00:11:53.137
of a difference in terms of
your employment prospects

00:11:53.137 --> 00:11:56.381
and certainly very little
in terms of what's actually

00:11:56.381 --> 00:11:58.263
taught at the law school.

00:11:58.263 --> 00:12:01.025
So you can do yourself a
huge favor by taking money

00:12:01.025 --> 00:12:04.659
for these slightly lower
ranked schools if that comes

00:12:04.659 --> 00:12:08.267
with more financial aid and
you'd probably be very happy

00:12:08.267 --> 00:12:11.875
to graduate debt free from
a top tier law school if the

00:12:11.875 --> 00:12:14.824
alternative was to go to
another top ranked law school

00:12:14.824 --> 00:12:16.812
with a ton of debt.

00:12:16.812 --> 00:12:19.369
Often that can be the
difference between zero debt

00:12:19.369 --> 00:12:24.076
and $250,000 worth of
debt and when you graduate

00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:27.294
if you don't go into big
law and you go into a

00:12:27.294 --> 00:12:30.752
legal career that pays,
you know, 70 or $80,000,

00:12:30.752 --> 00:12:33.711
which is the median
salary for an attorney,

00:12:33.711 --> 00:12:38.623
having or not having $250,000
worth of loans to repay

00:12:38.623 --> 00:12:41.650
over a 10 year time period
can make all the difference

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.147
in your quality of life.

00:12:43.147 --> 00:12:45.563
Again all things being
equal, go to a law school

00:12:45.563 --> 00:12:48.484
that is closer to the
geographical location that

00:12:48.484 --> 00:12:50.130
you know you want to practice.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.439
If you know that you want
to practice in Boston

00:12:52.439 --> 00:12:56.206
then by all means go to
a law school in Boston.

00:12:56.206 --> 00:12:58.961
It's very helpful to be
able to interview with a lot

00:12:58.961 --> 00:13:01.980
of firms in the area in which
you're going to law school.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.520
Otherwise the alternative
might be having to fly

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:07.095
across the country in
order to do the same number

00:13:07.095 --> 00:13:10.714
of interviews or to interview
with the same type of firm.

00:13:10.714 --> 00:13:12.845
What law schools don't tell
you is that at the beginning

00:13:12.845 --> 00:13:16.771
of your second year, you're
going to be doing a ton

00:13:16.771 --> 00:13:20.315
of interviews with firms
and governmental agencies

00:13:20.315 --> 00:13:23.498
to try and line up the job
that you have when you graduate

00:13:23.498 --> 00:13:27.167
from law school and it is
so much easier to be able

00:13:27.167 --> 00:13:30.774
to take on campus interviews
with the type of firms

00:13:30.774 --> 00:13:33.733
that you want to practice
in the future because local

00:13:33.733 --> 00:13:36.884
firms are more likely to
hold on campus interviews

00:13:36.884 --> 00:13:38.649
at a local law school.

00:13:38.649 --> 00:13:40.651
It's just the economics of the situation.

00:13:40.651 --> 00:13:44.038
So going to a law school
in the city or the state

00:13:44.038 --> 00:13:46.872
where you wanna practice
can make all the difference

00:13:46.872 --> 00:13:49.371
in your second year when
you're taking interviews

00:13:49.371 --> 00:13:52.860
for the firms that you wanna
work for in the future.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.685
So this is just the tip
of the iceberg in terms

00:13:55.685 --> 00:13:57.983
of what you should do before law school.

